  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A8DCE5">Example <span data-tag="A8DCE5">8.2.9.6</span>.</a> Let $\calJ $ be a Reedy category with respect to the factorization system $( \calJ ^{L}, \calJ ^{R})$. Then $\calJ ^{op}$ is a Reedy category with respect to the factorization system $( (\calJ ^ R)^{op}, (\calJ ^{L})^{op} )$. </p>
